# The knowledgebase, excluded per-directory rather than wholesale. It was once
# ignored entirely as "a self-contained Astro sub-project with its own tooling",
# but it is a Hugo site, there are no .astro files anywhere, and it carries no
# package.json or Prettier config — so nothing formatted it. That left
# kb/dev-docs/ unformatted while every other hand-authored markdown tree was
# not. Those pages are ordinary markdown and are now covered.
#
# Hugo layouts stay out: their Go template syntax (`{{ … }}`, `{{- /* … */ -}}`)
# is not HTML, and Prettier's html parser rewrites it destructively — 461 diff
# lines on kb/layouts/index.html alone, starting by collapsing the licence
# comment. Same failure class as the .hbs templates above.
kb/layouts/
# Hugo data files, both generated: api-symbols.json by the TypeDoc symbol-map
# plugin, legacy-slugs.json by utils/kb-redirects.mjs.
kb/data/
# The three generated trees under kb/ (#1632). All three are already ignored by
# kb/.gitignore, which does nothing here: Prettier's --ignore-path defaults to
# `.gitignore` and `.prettierignore` at the ROOT and never reads a nested
# .gitignore, so a tree ignored only from kb/ is invisible to git and fully
# visible to Prettier. That made `format:check` report on what had been built
# rather than on what had been written — clean before a knowledgebase build, 735
# warnings after `build:kb-content`, and a hard SyntaxError on minified HTML
# after `build:kb`. Restating them here is what actually excludes them, and
# tests/build/prettier-nested-gitignore.test.ts fails if a fourth is added there
# and not here.
#
# Assembled from assets/content/ + kb/dev-docs/ by utils/build-kb-content.mjs on
# every `npm run build:kb-content`; never committed.
kb/content/
